From 5718f684ce47256bede48bfe223e89ba6a4b90b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:15:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pi): keep the parent chain through tool results so a
 projected Pi session resumes with its history

A Pi session chains every entry to its predecessor, including the entries
the provider folds or drops: `toolResult` messages fold onto the assistant
that made the call, and model / thinking-level changes and labels are not
turns. An assistant whose `parentId` named one of those lost its parent in
the IR (the step DAG links turn to turn only), so every projection started a
new root at each tool call: Claude Code's `parentUuid` walk and Pi's own
main-thread walk both stopped at the last message, and `path resume` of a
Pi session showed the model nothing but the newest turn (measured: pi ->
claude and pi -> pi both answered from the new prompt alone).

- provider: resolve a turn's parent up to the nearest ancestor that is a
  turn.
- projector: a turn that followed an assistant with synthesized `-tr-N`
  tool-result entries now hangs off the last of those entries, matching
  how Pi files its own results, so the thread keeps every result.

Goldens recaptured: the six `-> pi` / `pi -> claude` outputs re-chain;
known defects unchanged.
